WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.177
These terms are often mixed together, so let us separate them.

00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:11.707
An L L M call is the simplest case: one input goes to a model and one response comes back.

00:00:11.707 --> 00:00:14.742
A workflow is a fixed sequence.

00:00:14.742 --> 00:00:19.202
For example, extract a value, validate it, and save it.

00:00:19.202 --> 00:00:21.225
The steps are already known.

00:00:21.846 --> 00:00:25.428
Classic rag is also usually a fixed workflow.

00:00:25.428 --> 00:00:31.098
We retrieve relevant documents, add them to the prompt, and generate an answer.

00:00:31.098 --> 00:00:41.103
An agent is different because the next step can depend on the current state or the result of a previous step.

00:00:41.103 --> 00:00:45.318
It might decide to call a tool, ask for clarification, generate, or stop.

00:00:45.318 --> 00:00:53.008
Agentic rag is a specific kind of agentic workflow where retrieval is inside that decision loop.

00:00:53.008 --> 00:01:00.224
The system can retrieve, grade the evidence, rewrite the query, try another source, or generate.

00:01:00.819 --> 00:01:05.636
Keeping these architectures separate helps you avoid unnecessary complexity.

00:01:05.636 --> 00:01:11.172
Do not call every workflow an agent just because an L L M appears somewhere inside it.
